WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.113 --> 00:00:01.290
(gun firing)

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:03.060
- [Narrator] This video
provided by Kyiv Police

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.710
shows officers shooting at drones

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.470
flying over the city in mid-October.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.720
The weapons can be seen
in multiple videos.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.790
Here, the device nose dives and explodes

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.500
near residential buildings.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.053
Several people were killed
in the attacks that day.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.160
Independent experts who
analyzed images from Ukraine

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.250
say Russia has been using
drones provided by Iran;

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:28.250
the Shahed-136 and its smaller
version, the Shahed-131.

00:00:28.357 --> 00:00:33.107
(Zelensky speaking in foreign language)

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.090
Ukraine is calling for new sanctions

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.340
and Western countries
say these drones show

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.740
Iran's direct involvement in the war.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.090
After initially denying it,

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.850
Iran acknowledged sending
some unmanned aerial vehicles,

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.760
or UAVs, to Russia before the invasion.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.060
Moscow has repeatedly denied
using the Iranian weapons,

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.470
but there are three types of clues

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.120
that confirm their origin:

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.770
the design, the way they move,

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.960
and the internal components
found among debris

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.583
by Ukrainian forces.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.490
First, let's take a closer
look at the structure

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:05.970
of the Iranian Shahed-131 and 136.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.770
They have a triangular shape with wings

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.428
and an arrow like extension
where the warhead is located.

00:01:11.428 --> 00:01:12.630
(Shahed swooshing)

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:14.310
The weapons, one of which is seen here

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.440
in Iranian Defense Ministry footage,

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.380
are self-destructing and
designed for one time use.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.903
Meaning after a strike,
they leave behind debris.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.500
These photos taken by
the news agency Reuters

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.330
show drone wreckage after an attack

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:30.030
on a fuel storage facility in Kharkiv.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:32.130
We ask analysts, including a drone expert

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.080
from the American organization CNA,

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.670
to review the images.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:39.030
They said these markings,
likely identification numbers,

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.620
are similar to those that can be seen

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.200
in Iranian handoff
footage of these drills.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.910
The debris found in Ukraine also have

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.290
some Russian lettering.

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.390
The letters can be seen
on the tips of the wings,

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.550
which appear to have the
same shape and structure

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.143
as the Iranian drones.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.660
In addition to their appearance,

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:58.620
analysts say the way
Shahed-136 and 131 drones move

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.630
is a distinct characteristic.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:02.880
Here's that footage from
Iran's Defense Ministry,

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.280
showing one of those
drones taking a sharp angle

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.170
before hitting a target.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:08.940
In a video posted to social media

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.370
from an October 17th attack in Kyiv

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:14.130
and verified by the news agency Storyful,

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.710
the drone can be seen
taking a similar sharp tilt

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:18.843
before it's obscured behind a building.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.960
Another video filmed
in Kyiv on the same day

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:26.062
shows a similar nose dive
maneuver before an explosion.

00:02:26.062 --> 00:02:27.420
(gentle music)

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.340
Key clues can also be found by looking

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:32.280
at the internal components
of these drones.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.690
On the right side is a photo that,

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.580
according to Israeli intelligence,

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.250
shows the engine of the Shahed-136 drone

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:41.490
being displayed in Iran in October 2014.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.010
We couldn't independently
verify the image.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.050
The analyst told us it looks consistent

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:47.970
with what Iran has disclosed.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.070
And on the left is a
Reuter's photo that shows

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.140
an engine recovered
from a strike in Ukraine

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.970
in October 2022.

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:55.890
Experts who review these images say

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:58.830
they both appear to be Mado MD550S,

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:02.550
the model that's used in
Shahed-136 Iranian drones.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.980
The copper color rotors
and general structure

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.870
are very similar.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:09.390
Other internal components
of drones found in Ukraine

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.850
can be linked to Iranian manufacturers,

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:14.160
according to Conflict Armament Research,

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.650
a private UK organization
that tracks illicit

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.750
arms and conflict zones.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.760
This panel, seen in a photo of debris

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.070
taken at the site of a strike in Ukraine,

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:25.050
contains the same layering of materials

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.150
as in other Iranian made UAVs,

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.950
according to the group.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.750
The group says this honeycomb meshing

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:33.960
is distinctive of Iranian
drones they've documented.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.808
It's this part sitting between
two layers of fiberglass

00:03:36.808 --> 00:03:39.240
which is meant to strengthen
the body of the weapon

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.160
without adding too much weight.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:43.020
Other Iranian characteristics include

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.060
handwritten serialization numbers

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.310
and stickers that can be
seen on the same panel,

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:49.263
said experts who viewed the pictures.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.550
Russia says it uses its
own drones in Ukraine,

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:55.500
but none of the known
models made in Russia

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.900
have the same characteristics
as the drones seen

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:00.630
in the Kyiv strikes,
according to analysts.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.940
The only self-destructing
drone of similar shape

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.220
that's produced in Russia is called KUB.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:08.250
It can be seen in this
Russian handout footage.

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:10.140
KUB drones couldn't be used in the strikes

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.000
on Kyiv in October, analyst say,

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.060
because they can't travel
farther than roughly 40 miles,

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.590
and Russian forces were stationed

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:20.250
more than a hundred miles away
from Kyiv on October 17th.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.530
In comparison, the Shahed
drones have a range

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:25.443
of at least 550 miles, according to Iran.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:30.240
The KUB is also smaller than the drones

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.580
Ukrainian officials say
were found in Ukraine.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.710
This still image of
Russian military footage

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.510
shows the scale of a KUB,

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:39.300
whereas this is the size of
the drones found in Ukraine

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.460
as seen in footage from
Ukrainian officials,

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.073
as well as images of
debris found in Kharkiv.

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:46.320
(gentle music)

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.270
Ukrainian officials
say Russia has launched

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:50.340
more than 300 Iranian drones

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.840
targeting civilian buildings,

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.060
as well as key energy infrastructure,

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.160
causing blackouts and
concerns about heating

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.360
ahead of winter.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.970
Kyiv says it was able to
shoot down many drones,

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:02.640
but is asking for more help from the West.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:04.590
Russia's Ministry of
Defense didn't respond

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.360
to a request for comment about the use

00:05:06.360 --> 00:05:08.253
of Iranian-made drones in the war.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:11.970
- We're also working
together to impose sanctions

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:14.820
on those supporting President Putin's war.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:15.843
That includes Iran.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:19.140
- [Narrator] The European
Union has already imposed

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:20.610
new sanctions on Iran,

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:23.940
and the US has hinted at
more penalties in the future.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:27.030
But these attacks also highlight
that despite sanctions,

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.250
in recent years, Iran has
built one of the world's

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.300
most successful drone fleets.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.883
(gentle music)

